{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonBoundary","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonBoundary","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Basic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.rhp_eq_iUnion_shifted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.rhp_eq_iUnion_shifted","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonBoundary.lean#L53-L62","doc":"The open right half-plane is the union of the shifted closed half-planes\n`{re ≥ ε}` over `ε > 0` — the set-level content of the ε-reduction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.eqOn_rhp_of_eqOn_shifted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.eqOn_rhp_of_eqOn_shifted","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonBoundary.lean#L41-L51","doc":"**The ε-reduction (boundary argument, load-bearing step).** If two functions\nagree on every shifted closed half-plane `{re ≥ ε}` for `ε > 0`, they agree\non the open half-plane `{re > 0}`. This is the `ε → 0` collapse of the\nWatson boundary limiting argument: it reduces uniqueness on `{re > 0}` (whose\nboundary point `0` breaks `DiffContOnCl` after transport) to uniqueness on\nthe shifted half-planes (which avoid that puncture). Pure `re`-order logic —\ntake `ε = re z`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}